  "operative_text": "SECTION 1 (TCA 39-17-1307(g)(1)): (1) The person is at least eighteen (18) years of age;\nSECTION 2 (TCA 39-17-1351(b)): If the applicant is at least eighteen (18) years of age and is not prohibited from possessing a firearm in this state pursuant to § 39-17-1307(b), 18 U.S.C. § 922(g), or any other state or federal law, and the applicant otherwise meets all of the requirements of this section, the department shall issue a permit to the applicant.\nSECTION 3 (TCA 39-17-1351(x)(1)): deleting the language \"twenty-one (21) years of age\" and substituting instead the language \"eighteen (18) years of age\".\nSECTION 4 (TCA 39-17-1313, new subsection (e)): (e) Notwithstanding subsection (a), this section does not apply to a person who is under twenty-one (21) years of age and transports or stores a firearm or firearm ammunition in the person's motor vehicle while on or utilizing a public or private parking"
}